   ],
   "skos:definition": "British cognitive psychologist at the University of Plymouth who co-introduced the idea of dual processes in reasoning with Peter Wason in 1975, proposed the heuristic-analytic theory, ran the classic belief-bias experiments and later helped redefine dual-process theory in terms of Type 1 and Type 2 processing.",
